From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radio: keep a started device's radio on or off as its
 configuration says

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: a modem that Aster disables must leave the mobile network and stay
         off it across Asterisk restarts, driver reconnects and modem resets,
         so that calls to a number shared with another SIM (a multi-SIM
         tariff) reach the other phone instead of a modem nobody answers
         (applies on top of 0003)

New device setting `radio = keep | on | off` (default keep: no AT+CFUN at
all, the upstream behaviour), read like every shared setting.

- off: right after ATE0 the initialization sends AT+CFUN? and AT+CFUN=0,
  then only the identity commands up to AT+CGSN, and stops there. The
  device stays connected (the monitor keeps pinging it) but is never
  initialized: no SIM commands, no SMS poll, no calls, no SMS. Its state
  reads "Radio off". Every reconnect (a driver restart, a reload, a modem
  that re-enumerated after a reset or a power cut) switches the radio off
  again, because the modems do not store AT+CFUN: a Quectel EC25-EUX and a
  Huawei E173 both come back from AT+CFUN=1,1 with +CFUN: 1, and the EC25
  also forgets AT+COPS=2.
- on: AT+CFUN? and AT+CFUN=1 right after ATE0, then the usual
  initialization, so a modem that was switched off comes back.
- 0 and not 4: 27.007 makes only 0 and 1 mandatory, and Huawei firmware
  treats 4 as an offline mode that refuses AT+CFUN=1 and AT+CFUN=0 until a
  reset (the E173 does exactly that), while 0 -> 1 works on both modems.
  A modem found in that offline mode counts as off for radio = off; for
  radio = on it is reset (AT+CFUN=1,1, written directly because the
  initialization task holds the queue) once, until AT+CFUN=1 succeeds again.
- the three commands carry ATQ_CMD_FLAG_IGNORE, so an ERROR does not drop
  the rest of the initialization task: a failed AT+CFUN? leaves the
  decision to AT+CFUN=<n>, and a refused AT+CFUN=0 of a modem already off
  goes on with the identity; every error that has to stop the
  initialization disconnects explicitly.
- a radio-off device does not open its UAC sound card, so a missing card
  cannot keep a disabled modem's radio on; the audio tty of a non-UAC
  device is still opened, because the monitor checks it. disconnect_quectel()
  closes what the connect opened rather than what the settings say now (a
  reload copies quec_uac into a running device) and clears the card handles.
- a radio-off device whose data tty does not exist (a disabled modem with
  fixed ports that is not plugged in) waits quietly: no "Trying to connect"
  and no "unable to open" line every discovery interval, which an idle
  appliance would otherwise write to its SD card.
- a change of `radio` restarts the device on reload, like `resetquectel`.
- +CFUN: is a classified response now (remembered in pvt->cfun); it is not
  unsolicited, so a QuectelAtCommand of AT+CFUN? still reports it as a Line.
- `quectel show device settings` prints Radio; QuectelDeviceEntry carries
  RadioSetting.
